## Foil CSS Effect (`.foil-shimmer`)

All foil visuals live in **`public/css/foil-effect.css`** — do not scatter foil styles elsewhere.

### How to apply

Add `.foil-shimmer` to the **wrapper element** of a card image, NOT the `<img>` itself:

```html
<!-- ✅ correct -->
<div class="card-image-wrap foil-shimmer"><img src="..."></div>

<!-- ❌ wrong — ::after won't render on a replaced element -->
<img class="foil-shimmer" src="...">
```

Apply the class when `card.is_foil === true`. Remove it otherwise.

### How to change the effect

Edit only `public/css/foil-effect.css`. Key knobs:
- Gradient angle (first arg to `linear-gradient`)
- Color stop positions and RGBA values
- `animation-duration` on `.foil-shimmer::after`
- `background-size` (larger = wider shimmer sweep)

### Foil button states

The deck editor Foil button always reads "Foil". State is visual only:
- `.foil-btn` — base (unpressed) appearance
- `.foil-btn--active` — pressed appearance when foil is selected for that card instance

---

## Collection Feature

The collection feature allows all authenticated users to manage their card collection.

### Access Control

All authenticated users (ADMIN, USER, GUEST) can access the collection interface.
The Collection button in the global navigation appears for all logged-in users.

### Data Persistence by Role

| Role | Storage | Persistence |
|------|---------|-------------|
| ADMIN, USER | PostgreSQL via API | Permanent, server-synced |
| GUEST | localStorage | Session-only sandbox |

### GUEST Sandbox Mode

GUEST users operate in a **sandbox mode** where:
- Collection data is stored in `localStorage` under key `guestCollection`
- No API calls are made for GUEST collection operations
- A sandbox banner is displayed explaining the non-persistent nature
- Users are prompted to sign up for permanent storage

### Key Functions in `public/js/collection-view.js`

| Function | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `isGuestUser()` | Returns truthy if current user has GUEST role |
| `loadGuestCollectionFromStorage()` | Retrieves GUEST collection from localStorage |
| `saveGuestCollectionToStorage(cards)` | Persists GUEST collection to localStorage |
| `showGuestSandboxBanner()` | Displays the sandbox notification banner |

### localStorage Schema

```js
// Key: 'guestCollection'
// Value: JSON array of collection cards
[
  {
    card_id: string,
    card_type: string,      // 'character', 'special', etc.
    quantity: number,
    image_path: string,
    card_data: {            // Required for display
      name: string,
      set_number: string
    }
  }
]
```

### API Endpoints (ADMIN/USER only)

All endpoints require authentication. GUEST users bypass these via localStorage.

| Method | Endpoint | Description |
|--------|----------|-------------|
| GET | `/api/collections/me` | Fetch user's collection |
| GET | `/api/collections/me/cards` | Fetch collection cards |
| POST | `/api/collections/me/cards` | Add card to collection |
| PUT | `/api/collections/me/cards/:cardId` | Update card quantity |
| DELETE | `/api/collections/me/cards/:cardId` | Remove card from collection |
| GET | `/api/collections/me/history` | Fetch collection change history |

### Frontend Flow

```
loadCollection()
    │
    ├─ isGuestUser()? ──yes──► loadGuestCollectionFromStorage()
    │                         showGuestSandboxBanner()
    │
    └─ no ──► fetch('/api/collections/me/cards')
```

### Files

| Layer | File |
|-------|------|
| Frontend JS | `public/js/collection-view.js` |
| Frontend CSS | `public/css/collection-view.css` |
| HTML Template | (rendered via EJS in `src/index.ts`) |
| Backend API | Collection endpoints in `src/index.ts` |
| Repository | `src/database/collectionRepository.ts` |
| Service | `src/services/collectionService.ts` |

### Testing

| Test Type | Location |
|-----------|----------|
| Unit tests | `tests/unit/collection-view.test.ts`, `tests/unit/collectionService.test.ts` |
| Integration tests | `tests/integration/collection/*.test.ts` |

Key test suites:
- **collection-admin-access.test.ts** — verifies all roles can access collection APIs
- **collection-workflow.test.ts** — end-to-end collection operations
- **collection-view.test.ts** — unit tests for GUEST sandbox functions
- **collection-guest-sandbox-ui.test.ts** — verifies signup link behavior

### Adding Features

When modifying the collection feature:
1. Update both API and localStorage paths if applicable
2. Ensure GUEST users receive appropriate feedback (no server errors)
3. Update both unit and integration tests
4. Test with all three roles: ADMIN, USER, GUEST

---

## Login/Signup Modal Pattern

The application uses a **modal-based** login/signup flow, NOT separate page routes.

### Key Points

- **No `/signup` route exists** — signup is part of the login modal
- **No `/login` route exists** — login is displayed via a modal overlay
- Use `showLoginModal()` to display the login view
- Use `showSignupModal()` to display the signup view

### Available Functions (in `public/js/auth-app-init.js`)

| Function | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `showLoginModal()` | Opens modal with login view visible |
| `showSignupModal()` | Opens modal with signup view visible |
| `showLoginError(msg)` | Displays error in login form |
| `hideLoginError()` | Hides login error message |
| `showSignupError(msg)` | Displays error in signup form |
| `hideSignupError()` | Hides signup error message |

### Linking to Signup

**DO NOT** use `href="/signup"` — it will 404.

Instead, use a click handler:

```javascript
// ✅ Correct approach
link.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    e.preventDefault();
    showSignupModal();
});

// ❌ Wrong - /signup does not exist
<a href="/signup">Sign up</a>
```

### Modal HTML Structure

The login modal lives in `public/components/login/login.html` and contains:
- `#loginModal` — outer container
- `#loginView` — login form (username/password)
- `#signupView` — signup form (username/email/password/confirm)

Only one view is visible at a time, controlled by `style.display`.

### Related Files

| Purpose | File |
|---------|------|
| Modal HTML template | `public/components/login/login.html` |
| Modal JS (event handlers) | `public/components/login/login.js` |
| Global auth functions | `public/js/auth-app-init.js` |
| Auth service | `public/js/auth-service.js` |
| Unit tests | `tests/unit/auth-app-init.test.ts` |

---

## Google Sign-In / Firebase Admin Setup

The application supports Google Sign-In using Firebase Admin SDK for server-side ID token verification.

### Architecture

- **Frontend**: Uses Firebase Client SDK to trigger Google Sign-In popup and obtain ID token
- **Backend**: Uses `firebase-admin` to verify the ID token via `verifyIdToken()`
- **No Cloud Storage**: We only use Firebase for authentication, NOT for `@google-cloud/storage` or any other Google Cloud services

### Key Files

| Layer | File |
|-------|------|
| Firebase config | `src/config/firebaseAdmin.ts` |
| Auth service | `src/services/AuthenticationService.ts` |
| Frontend auth | `public/js/auth-service.js` |
| Integration tests | `tests/integration/google-auth-firebase.test.ts` |

### Environment Variables

| Variable | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON` | JSON string of Firebase service account credentials |

For local dev, can also use file: `infra/firebase-service-account.json`

### Dependency Chain Issue

The `firebase-admin` package pulls in `@google-cloud/storage` which has a deep dependency chain:

```
firebase-admin
  → @google-cloud/storage
    → teeny-request
      → http-proxy-agent@5.x
        → @tootallnate/once@2.x (VULNERABLE)
```

**Important**: We do NOT use `@google-cloud/storage` functionality. Firebase Admin is used solely for `verifyIdToken()` in Google Sign-In. The vulnerable code path (`@tootallnate/once`) is never executed in our usage.

---

## Trivy CI Configuration

### Known Issue: trivy-action Ignores .trivyignore

The `aquasecurity/trivy-action` GitHub Action has [documented bugs](https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy-action/issues/436) where:
- The `TRIVY_IGNOREFILE` environment variable doesn't work
- The `trivyignores` input parameter doesn't reliably pass the ignore file to Trivy

**Solution**: Use Trivy CLI directly instead of the GitHub Action.

### Current Configuration (deploy.yml)

```yaml
- name: Install Trivy
  run: |
    sudo apt-get update
    sudo apt-get install -y wget apt-transport-https gnupg lsb-release
    wget -qO - https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy-repo/deb/public.key | gpg --dearmor | sudo tee /usr/share/keyrings/trivy.gpg > /dev/null
    echo "deb [signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/trivy.gpg] https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy-repo/deb $(lsb_release -sc) main" | sudo tee -a /etc/apt/sources.list.d/trivy.list
    sudo apt-get update
    sudo apt-get install -y trivy

- name: Run Trivy vulnerability scanner
  run: |
    trivy fs \
      --ignorefile .trivyignore \
      --severity CRITICAL,HIGH,MEDIUM,LOW,UNKNOWN \
      --exit-code 1 \
      --ignore-unfixed \
      --scanners vuln \
      .
```

### .trivyignore File

Located at project root. Format: one CVE ID per line with comments explaining the suppression reason.

```
# CVE-XXXX-YYYY: Package Name - Brief description
# Suppressed because: [reason]
# Review periodically: [what to check]
CVE-XXXX-YYYY
```

### Currently Suppressed CVEs

| CVE | Package | Reason |
|-----|---------|--------|
| CVE-2026-3449 | @tootallnate/once | Vulnerable code path never executed - we only use firebase-admin for `verifyIdToken()`, not `@google-cloud/storage` or proxy functionality |

### Adding New Suppressions

1. Add the CVE ID to `.trivyignore` with full documentation:
   - CVE ID and package name
   - CVSS score and severity
   - Why it's safe to suppress (what code path is/isn't executed)
   - What blocks the fix (upstream dependency issues)
   - When to review (what upstream change would allow removal)
2. The CI will automatically pick it up via `--ignorefile .trivyignore`

### Key Files

| Purpose | File |
|---------|------|
| Ignore file | `.trivyignore` |
| CI workflow | `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` (trivy job) |
| Documentation | `docs/trivy-dependency-scanning.md` |
